BOARDING PASS PRINTER

Boarding Pass Printer — a real-world task using only today's concepts: for loops, range(), looping a fixed number of times, reusing input(), while validation, comparisons, if / elif / else, variables, and printing. No imports, no tricks.

Solve it individually, then come together as a group to compare approaches. Good luck!

A small airline runs an early-morning shuttle from Port Harcourt to Lagos with 30 seats. At the check-in desk, the agent types how many passengers are on the manifest and the counter printer produces one boarding pass line per passenger, with seats assigned in order starting from Seat 1.

The program must:
- Ask "Passengers on manifest: " and keep asking until the number is at least 1 and at most 30 (reuse your while validation from last week).
- Then, one passenger at a time in order, ask the passenger's name and immediately print their boarding pass line in this shape: Passenger 1: Adaeze - Seat 1
- After the last passenger, print: TOTAL PASSENGERS: 3
- Seats must start from Seat 1, never Seat 0.

Sample run:

Passengers on manifest: 12
Passengers on manifest: 3
Passenger 1 name: Adaeze
Passenger 2 name: Emeka
Passenger 3 name: Fatima

Passenger 1: Adaeze - Seat 1
Passenger 2: Emeka - Seat 2
Passenger 3: Fatima - Seat 3
TOTAL PASSENGERS: 3

Edge cases to handle: a manifest of exactly 1 (a single pass), a manifest of exactly 30 (a full shuttle), an entry of 0 and an entry of 31 for the manifest (both rejected, asked again), and checking that the seat number of the last passenger equals the manifest size.
